Success stories don´t just happen. They are made...
Make it happen! We are looking forward to your application!

Bosch Engineering Center Cluj is offering scholarships of 4000 RON/month over the academic year for enthusiastic enthusiastic Doctoral students. Students granted with scholarships have the possibility to work together with Bosch experts in Software and Hardware fields.
The research topics we are proposing to be approached together are:
• AI embedded / edge AI;
• AI chips design;
• Neural networks optimizations;
• HW friendly AI architecture;
• Knowledge distillation from large to small embedded models;
• Real-time physical AI;
• AI training HW and training optimization techniques (stretched objective);
• Hardware-Software co-design.
• Student in a full-time doctoral program;
• Year of study: 2nd, 3rd;
• Having the annual doctoral studies conditions met: articles, conference, etc;
• Attending to one of the following research domains: Computers and Information Technology, Systems Engineering, Electronic Engineering, Telecommunications and Information Technologies, Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering;
• Not enroled in public funded projects.
Selection:
• Submit your CV until the 31st of October;
• Technical interview period between 1st of November – 14th of November;
• The subject of doctoral thesis must be in line with one of the topics proposed;
• For more information contact us on ECCAcademicPrograms@ro.bosch.com.
Benefits of being in the Bosch Scholarship Program:
• Scholarship of 4000 RON/month;
• Mentorship for a project developed together;
• Access to educational resources within Bosch;
• Networking possibilities with IT experts.

